course: dictionary
lesson: 9320
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it, which are its context. «The sperm whale clicked in the deep sea.» The word whale comes right after sperm, so here sperm is the name of a kind of whale.
explain: Now read this: «A sperm joins with an egg cell to start a new living thing.» Here sperm means a tiny male cell. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if I swap in my meaning? Whale does not fit with egg cells, so the cell meaning is the right one.
explain: Many sentences about the sea and sea animals use sperm as part of a name, while science lessons use it for cells. Read the whole sentence before you decide. If you are still not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A sperm is a tiny male cell made by male animals and men.
fact: When a sperm joins with an egg cell from a female, a new baby animal or baby human can start to grow.
fact: In plants, male cells that join with egg cells are carried in pollen.
fact: The sperm whale is named after a waxy substance in its head that people long ago wrongly thought was sperm.
fact: «The sperm whale makes the loudest sound of any animal» is a true sentence about a whale, not a cell.
exercise: «The sperm whale clicked in the deep sea.» In this sentence, what is sperm part of? | A tiny male cell | A fish's egg | A plant's pollen | *The name of a kind of whale
exercise: In plants, what carries the male cells that join with egg cells? | Roots | Petals | Water | *Pollen
exercise: «A sperm joins with an egg cell.» What can start to grow after this? | A stone on the beach | A cloud in the sky | A new leaf on a tree | *A new baby animal or baby human
test: What do a sperm cell and an egg cell do together? | *Join to start a new living thing | Turn into rain | Carry pollen away from flowers | Make a loud click under the sea
test: Why is the sperm whale named that? | It eats only pollen | *People long ago wrongly thought a waxy substance in its head was sperm | It lives on a farm | Its tail looks like a sperm
exam: In «Sperm whales nap upright near the surface», what tells you that sperm means a kind of whale? | The word surface | Nothing, you must guess | *The word whales right after it | The word nap
